minals and keep the W sequence for potential chow.  \n\nReason: T1 is a terminal and isolated; keeping W1-W2-W3 offers more flexibility to form a chow with W4. Discarding J3 is also okay, but J3 has only 2 left, making a pung unlikely, but it's an honor that could pair if I draw another. However, I need a pair for winning, so keeping J3 as a potential pair candidate is reasonable. But I have no other J3, so it's just a single.  \n\nActually, I need a pair, so keeping any tile that has more copies left might help. W2 has 3 left, W3 has 3 left, W1 has 4 left, T1 has 2 left, J3 has 2 left. All have some chance.  \n\nBut discarding T1 removes a terminal and doesn't break a potential sequence in my hand.  \n\nFinal choice: Play T1.  \n\nAnswer: Play T1"}
